            0.41,
            0.087,
            0.89,
            0.173
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "this point. Then, draw a line parallel to the X-axis from the point corresponding to distance 20 m on the Y-axis. The point where these two lines intersect represents the position 20 m at time t = 1 s on the graph (Fig. 4.11b)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.368,
            0.172,
            0.89,
            0.223
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) Similarly, plot on the graph paper all points corresponding to positions of the vehicle at different instants of time."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.346,
            0.226,
            0.89,
            0.278
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "7. Once all points are plotted, connect them to create the position-time graph for the vehicle’s motion (Fig. 4.11c). It is a straight line for the data given in Table 4.3."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.333,
            0.281,
            0.889,
            0.333
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This was an example of plotting a position-time graph. Similar procedure can be used to plot the other graphs which you will be learning ahead."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.12,
            0.353,
            0.176,
            0.37
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Note"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.38,
            0.284,
            0.505
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Remember, a graph is not a route map. It does not show the route but how the position of the object changes with time with respect to the origin."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.327,
            0.332,
            0.385,
            0.393
          ],
          "content": [
